<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Nov 16.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Nov 16.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Nov 16</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE %   BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   220	   0.30     342450  75.34     7.11</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   168	   0.22     393500  66.11     6.83</p>
<p>ACC		   1390	   1.56	22320  28.24     5.85</p>
<p>Tata Power	   119	   0.16     170500  20.29     7.01</p>
<p>IPCL		   109	   0.04     108700  11.85     1.91</p>
<p>ICICI		   58	   0.07     168800   9.79     6.29</p>
<p>Andhra Valley	100	   0.15	94800   9.48     7.82</p>
<p>Tata Chem	    200	   0.27	35050   7.01     7.04</p>
<p>Arvind Mills	 114	   0.14	46000   5.24     6.40</p>
<p>Sterlite	     185	   0.22	12700   2.35     6.20</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 6.75 percent on an annualised basis against 13.45 percent in the carry forward account ended Nov 2.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
